TurboFieldfare is a specialized inference runtime for Gemma 4 26B-A4B, engineered to operate within an extreme memory constraint of approximately 2 GB on Apple Silicon Macs. The central design challenge is fitting a 26-billion-parameter model into this budget, which is achieved by keeping only the shared core weights and FP16 KV cache resident in RAM while streaming expert weights directly from SSD storage.

The runtime employs a hybrid execution model. Metal kernels handle attention and routing calculations using resident weights. The CPU then identifies the top-8 required experts via the router and manages an LFU cache. Cache misses